-- examples/checks/agg-rederived-1-given.rofl — A FACT THAT IS GIVEN AND ALSO DERIVED SAYS SO AFTER EVERY EVALUATION.
--
-- `seen(a)` is asserted and a rule concludes it too. The firing is recorded
-- with a `derived_by` row, and the two must stand or go together. Until
-- 2026-09-28 clearing the derived layer dropped the row and kept the firing on
-- the base fact, so the next evaluation found the firing "not new" and never
-- wrote the row again. The facts/agg.rofl ledger is what first showed it:
-- `ignored(...)` is asserted and re-derived from `claim(ignored, ...)`.
--
-- TWO FILES, NUMBERED, because the TypeScript host evaluates on every `load`
-- and a world's files are loaded in sorted order: this one is evaluated alone
-- first, and agg-rederived-2-read.rofl, loaded after it, makes the second
-- evaluation and reads the rows it leaves. The other order checks nothing.
--
-- `seen(b)` is derived through `relayed`, which is derived too, so the old
-- firing on it also cited a fact the clearing removed.

edb(given).
edb(seen).
given(a).
given(b).
seen(a).
seen(b).

seen(X)    :- given(X), X = a.
relayed(X) :- given(X), X = b.
seen(X)    :- relayed(X).
